@startuml sequence-relations
!theme plain

title Relations: Content, Trust, and Typing

participant "MCP Client" as Client
participant "Gateway" as Gateway
database "Store" as DB

== Content Relation (Fragment to Fragment) ==

note over Client
  Relation types for content:
  SUPPORTS, CONTRADICTS, EXTENDS,
  SUPERSEDES, DERIVED_FROM, RELATED_TO,
  EXAMPLE_OF
end note

Client -> Client: Create Relation\n{from: fragment-A,\n to: fragment-B,\n by: agent,\n type: SUPPORTS,\n content: "A provides evidence for B"}
Client -> Client: Sign relation

Client -> Gateway: POST /api/v1/relations
activate Gateway
Gateway -> Gateway: Validate addresses\nand relation type
Gateway -> DB: CreateRelation
DB --> Gateway: OK
Gateway --> Client: 201 Created\n{relation}
deactivate Gateway

== Typing Relation (Self-Reference) ==

note over Client
  Typing relation types:
  QUESTION, HYPOTHESE,
  ANTITHESE, SYNTHESE
  
  To = empty or same as From
end note

Client -> Client: Create Relation\n{from: fragment-X,\n to: {},\n by: agent,\n type: HYPOTHESE}
Client -> Client: Sign relation

Client -> Gateway: POST /api/v1/relations
activate Gateway
Gateway -> DB: CreateRelation
DB --> Gateway: OK
Gateway --> Client: 201 Created\n{relation}
deactivate Gateway

== Trust Relation ==

note over Client
  TRUST relation expresses
  agent's trust/distrust
  in an entity (Fragment or Agent)
end note

Client -> Client: Create Relation\n{from: fragment-Y,\n to: {},\n by: agent,\n type: TRUST,\n content: "I verified this is correct"}
Client -> Client: Sign relation

Client -> Gateway: POST /api/v1/relations
activate Gateway
Gateway -> DB: CreateRelation
DB --> Gateway: OK
Gateway --> Client: 201 Created\n{relation}
deactivate Gateway

== Query Relations by Type ==

Client -> Gateway: GET /api/v1/relations?type=TRUST
activate Gateway
Gateway -> DB: ListRelations(type=TRUST)
DB --> Gateway: [Relation, ...]
Gateway --> Client: 200 OK\n[relations]
deactivate Gateway

== Query Relations for Entity ==

Client -> Gateway: GET /api/v1/entities/{addr}/relations
activate Gateway
Gateway -> DB: GetRelationsForEntity(addr)
note right of DB
  Searches both from_json
  and to_json fields
end note
DB --> Gateway: [Relation, ...]
Gateway --> Client: 200 OK\n[relations]
deactivate Gateway

== Build Trust Score (Client-side) ==

Client -> Client: Load my Agent with TrustStore
Client -> Gateway: GET /api/v1/relations?type=TRUST
Gateway --> Client: [all TRUST relations]

Client -> Client: For target entity:
note right of Client
  1. Find TRUST relations pointing to entity
  2. For each relation:
     - Get asserting agent (relation.by)
     - Look up my trust in that agent
     - Weight: my_trust * their_trust
  3. Sum weighted trusts
  4. Normalize to [-1.0, 1.0]
end note

Client -> Client: effective_trust =\nΣ(my_trust[agent] × agent_trusts_entity)

== Refinement Relations ==

note over Client
  Refinement relation types:
  SPECIALIZES, CLARIFIES, GENERALIZES
end note

Client -> Client: Create Relation\n{from: detailed-fragment,\n to: general-fragment,\n by: agent,\n type: SPECIALIZES}
Client -> Client: Sign relation

Client -> Gateway: POST /api/v1/relations
activate Gateway
Gateway -> DB: CreateRelation
Gateway --> Client: 201 Created
deactivate Gateway

@enduml
